english:
(a) Factorise the determinant $\left| \begin{array}{ccc} a & b & b \\ b & a & b \\ b & b & a \end{array} \right|$. (6 marks)
(b) Let $a$ be real. Given the system in $x,y,z$, $(E):\begin{cases}ax+y+z=1\\x+ay+z=a\\x+y+az=a^2\end{cases}$, find the values of $a$ for which $(E)$ has:
(i) a unique solution;
(ii) infinitely many solutions;
(iii) no solution. (8 marks)
(c) Let $a=2$. Solve $(E)$. (6 marks)
